# Model and Research

The current task and `roadmap.md` define the research question. Gear labels and closed-stage notes in `docs/strategy-gears.md` preserve experiment history; they do not, by themselves, authorize a change or prohibit a new explicitly requested experiment.

- Keep offline simulation separate from private APIs, live order routing, and production deployment.
- State data source, time period, configuration, execution assumptions, fees, and treatment of pending/open-at-end positions.
- Distinguish signal from fill when execution latency is part of the contract.
- Preserve baseline behavior when new flags are off where applicable; record intentional baseline changes.
- Keep code correctness, experimental evidence, and claims about strategy performance distinct.
- Use independent episode/time splits when selecting parameters; do not choose on the reported test set.
- Coordinate separately if a task changes the D producer, shared data contract, or B consumer. Do not make those changes implicitly.

Choose tests and review to match the changed assumption. A small research bugfix does not require VPS validation or a full agent chain.
